  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "The Feishu UI for DeepSeek Harness (dsh)",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](LICENSE)\n[](package.json)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@dsh-feishu/dsh-feishu)\n[](.github/workflows/ci.yml)\n\nThe Feishu UI for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (dsh) — a dsh-native plugin with a **panel-driven control console**: every slash command is a button on the ⚙️ control-panel card, approvals and questions resolve inside the chat, and one QR scan sets the whole app up."
    },
    {
      "section": "The Feishu UI for DeepSeek Harness (dsh)",
      "text": "> **Note:** [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) is\n> still pre-release and may break between releases. dsh-feishu is built and\n> verified against **dsh `@latest`** — currently **`0.2.1-rc.2`** — both when\n> installed from npm and from git.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e9163793-52f2-4e2c-a08a-22b27372be61\n\n*2.5-min demo: control panel, streaming card, approval and question.*"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from npm",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Windows: https://nodejs.org  (or: winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS)",
      "text": "node --version"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. install pnpm",
      "text": "npm install -g pnpm"
    },
    {
      "section": "--allow-build=protobufjs lets pnpm run it)",
      "text": "npx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile feishu add @dsh-feishu/dsh-feishu@latest --allow-build=protobufjs"
    },
    {
      "section": "4. one QR scan — create + configure the Feishu app",
      "text": "npx --yes --package @dsh-feishu/dsh-feishu dsh-feishu-setup --new --profile feishu"
    },
    {
      "section": "5. run",
      "text": "npx @deepseek-ai/dsh --profile feishu\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from source",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Windows: https://nodejs.org  (or: winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS)",
      "text": "node --version"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. install pnpm",
      "text": "npm install -g pnpm"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. clone and build",
      "text": "git clone https://github.com/PGZXB/dsh-feishu.git\ncd dsh-feishu\npnpm install\npnpm run build"
    },
    {
      "section": "4. install into a profile",
      "text": "npx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile feishu add link:."
    },
    {
      "section": "5. one QR scan — create + configure the Feishu app",
      "text": "pnpm run setup:feishu -- --new --profile feishu"
    },
    {
      "section": "6. run",
      "text": "npx @deepseek-ai/dsh --profile feishu\n```\n\nThen message the bot in Feishu. The setup wizard handles the Feishu app end\nto end — no web-console work and no manual credentials. Already have an app?\nSet `FEISHU_APP_ID` / `FEISHU_APP_SECRET` (environment or profile config)\ninstead — see [docs/feishu-setup.md](docs/feishu-setup.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Uninstall",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "remove the plugin from the profile",
      "text": "npx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile feishu remove @dsh-feishu/dsh-feishu"
    },
    {
      "section": "(paths shown for the default dsh home, ~/.dsh)",
      "text": "rm -rf ~/.dsh/profiles/feishu ~/.dsh/feishu\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "A Feishu chat is a dsh session — the bot is the agent's avatar. A typical\nsession goes like this:\n\n1. **Start a chat.** Direct-message the bot, or run `/group <name>` to\n   create a group the bot joins. In a group, @-mention the bot (the\n   default policy; a group with just you and the bot also answers plain\n   messages, and the policy is configurable).\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"docs/assets/snapshots/1_chat.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"Chat with the bot\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "2. **Open the control panel.** Send `/panel` to pop up the panel card.\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"docs/assets/snapshots/2_panel.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"Control panel\"></p>\n\n3. **Pick a working directory.** The bot refuses work until the chat has\n   one: tap **📚 Pick project** to choose from a list (the `/repo`\n   equivalent), or **📁 Change dir** to type a path (the `/cd <path>`\n   equivalent).\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"docs/assets/snapshots/3_repo.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"Project picker\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "4. **Ask.** Send a message — the agent runs and its output streams into a\n   live card (tool calls, reasoning, markdown, tables). The card ends green\n   with the full answer inside; Stop, copy, retry, and the ⚙️ panel button\n   sit on it.\n\n| Mid-stream | Finalized |\n   |---|---|\n   |  |  |\n\n5. **Approve or answer when asked.** A permission escalation posts an\n   approval card — tap **Allow once** (or **Reject**). A question posts a\n   card you answer with a tap (or a reply)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "| Approval | Question |\n   |---|---|\n   |  |  |\n\n6. **Manage sessions.** Tap **🗂️ Sessions** to list saved sessions and\n   resume any of them from the card (the `/sessions` equivalent; `/resume\n   <id>` moves one into this chat), and tap **➕ New chat** (the `/clear`\n   equivalent) to start fresh without deleting the old one.\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"docs/assets/snapshots/6_sessions.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"Sessions picker\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Every button on the panel card maps to a slash command — pick whichever\nfeels faster; `/help` lists them all."
    },
    {
      "section": "Commands",
      "text": "| Command | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| `/help` | list all commands |\n| `/panel` | open the control-panel card (all commands as buttons) |\n| `/group <name>` | create a group with the bot (bare opens a name-input card) |\n| `/cancel` | stop the running turn |\n| `/cd <path>` | set this chat's working directory (bare opens a path-input card) |\n| `/repo [path]` | pick a project directory (bare scans the default roots; `/repo <path>` scans that path) |\n| `/status` | show this chat's session status |\n| `/feishu-status` | show the surface diagnostic card |\n| `/schedule` | list active reminders |\n| `/model <provider/model>` | switch this session's model (bare opens the picker) |\n| `/export` | send this chat's session log as a file |\n| `/log` | send the dsh-feishu log file to this chat (handy for debugging — please attach the key log lines when you file an issue) |\n| `/sessions` | list saved sessions (resume any of them from the card) |\n| `/resume <id>` | resume a saved session (bare opens the session list) |\n| `/clear` `/new` | start a fresh conversation (the old session stays saved) |\n| `/goal <text>` | set the task goal (bare opens a text-input card) |\n| `/compact` | compact older conversa"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Live streaming cards** — tool calls, reasoning, markdown, and tables stream in as the agent works.\n- **One-tap control panel** — `/panel` renders the full command palette as buttons; no command syntax to remember, and each button is the exact equivalent of typing the command.\n- **In-card approvals & questions** — approve a permission escalation or answer the agent's questions in the chat.\n- **Sessions survive restarts** — a chat's session and its working directory are persisted across daemon restarts; `/sessions` lists, resumes, renames, archives, and exports them.\n- **One-QR quick setup** — a single Feishu QR scan creates and configures the app (bot profile, scopes, event subscriptions, credentials) and writes the dsh profile.\n- **Files in both directions** — images, files, videos, and rich-text posts you send land in the workspace as plain files the agent reads by path; the agent can send workspace files and images back to the chat.\n- **Message queue & steering** — messages sent while a turn is running queue visibly; edit, delete, or steer them into the running turn.\n- **Files a turn produced** — appear as chips at the bottom of the card; tap one to receive it in the chat.\n- "
    },
    {
      "section": "Contributing",
      "text": "See [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).\nDevelopment, tests, and release: [docs/development.md](docs/development.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Community",
      "text": "Join the dsh-feishu community group on Feishu:\n\n<img src=\"docs/assets/feishu-group-qr-code.png\" alt=\"dsh-feishu community group QR code\" width=\"220\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "Credits",
      "text": "- **[botmux](https://github.com/deepcoldy/botmux)** — the reference for the\n  group-chat interaction patterns: streaming cards, approvals, and the\n  QR-driven Open Platform quick-setup flow. dsh-feishu borrows botmux's\n  *interaction and onboarding patterns*, not its architecture — botmux\n  bridges external CLIs, while this surface is dsh-native and in-process.\n- **[DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)** —\n  the platform this surface is built for.\n- **[Lark Open Platform SDK](https://github.com/larksuite/node-sdk)** — the\n  WebSocket long connection and card APIs the transport builds on."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE)."
    }
